Cell["\<\
Table 4 provides several examples of compressing digits with indexed \
concatenation. We note here that the common overline notation looks much \
simpler, and probably should be retained except in cases such as the last \
example, which is an irrational number. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.942436580204573*^9, 3.942436593632391*^9}, {
