Cell["\<\
Again, the concatenation of lists is a list, without adding nested levels of \
the list structure. Of course, to make a list with sublists, we can nest the \
lists that serve as input to the concatenation operator. A concatenation of \
lists with one level of sublists is a list with one level of sublists:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.938273844415525*^9, 3.938273868977188*^9}, {
   3.938273904089712*^9, 3.9382739266943073`*^9}, {3.9419391417538223`*^9, 
