Cell["\<\
The above examples have primarily involved increasing values, increasing \
number of values, or both. However, because any formula based on the \
concatenation indices can be used, this notation can also represent sequences \
involving descending numbers of elements and descending values .\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.943349630341303*^9, 3.943349632244825*^9}, {
   3.943350780331805*^9, 3.943350805497497*^9}, {3.94335086651382*^9, 
