Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9 Conclusions", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.842968201150871*^9, 3.84296820179364*^9}, {
   3.851975315164182*^9, 3.851975320827327*^9}, {3.852839262757098*^9, 
   3.852839276556146*^9}, {3.923407217558078*^9, 3.923407259535666*^9}, {
   3.93127410231599*^9, 3.931274104374205*^9}, {3.9312741793733177`*^9, 
   3.931274183507604*^9}, {3.931277818955561*^9, 3.931277820029943*^9}, {
   3.9337708561152096`*^9, 3.933770856127341*^9}, {3.9356763229562263`*^9, 
   3.935676326530073*^9}, {3.936125390729555*^9, 3.936125429372444*^9}, {
   3.941988551217835*^9, 3.9419885546780396`*^9}, {3.947160957155072*^9, 
   3.947160957297665*^9}, {3.947161056352934*^9, 3.947161073920044*^9}, {
   3.947278748793289*^9, 3.947278751177096*^9}, 3.947341595260191*^9, 
   3.9478613753650074`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"cecd0815-2ae6-4a70-9f2c-\
ead772856462"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Throughout the history of mathematics and science, good notation has \
contributed to increased understanding, greater insights, and more rapid and \
successful advancement in the field under study. Examples include the decimal \
system (replacing previous use of Roman numerals and dependence on \
fractions), Leibnitz\[CloseCurlyQuote] representation of the derivative of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["y", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "83a59938-0454-9748-bdd2-ad404d07b28e"],
 " with respect to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["x", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "06e5ed17-281e-e148-9a16-b106f3dff9a3"],
 " as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "y"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "504deaf7-aeac-9242-b7ed-e8bc17fcd7cc"],
 ", vector notation to conveniently describe relationships in \
three-dimensional space, the 4-vector notation in Special Relativity to \
include the time coordinate, and the summation convention used in tensor \
calculus and General Relativity. Good notation facilitates good work."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.941988685165859*^9, 3.941988693470001*^9}, {
   3.947278774433069*^9, 3.947278992810414*^9}, {3.947279053518284*^9, 
   3.947279414069689*^9}, {3.947279464887099*^9, 3.947279469665022*^9}, {
   3.94734108256975*^9, 3.947341135713878*^9}, {3.947341214180325*^9, 
   3.947341223488285*^9}, 
   3.9478621661541195`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"52a510a2-43a7-b641-ba0a-\
48f7e57b052b"],

Cell["\<\
The Indexed Concatenation Notation, following the lead of other indexed \
operators, allows compact representations of strings, lists, sequences, \
integer lists, matrices, and other similar expressions, examples of which we \
have considered above. It capitalizes on repetitions, periodicities and other \
patterns to compress information into a reduced form. It may be hoped that \
such notation summarizing internal patterns may not only serve as a new means \
of information compression, but also contribute to simpler and more \
insightful use of the data.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.941988685165859*^9, 3.941988693470001*^9}, {
  3.947278774433069*^9, 3.947278992810414*^9}, {3.947279053518284*^9, 
  3.947279318120476*^9}, {3.94727941819594*^9, 3.947279422904127*^9}, {
  3.947279483273918*^9, 3.9472798099134808`*^9}, {3.94734125223884*^9, 
  3.9473412751715927`*^9}, {3.9473413134629307`*^9, 3.94734138329632*^9}, {
  3.94734185086957*^9, 3.947341889691492*^9}, {3.947341951202923*^9, 
  3.947341979754631*^9}, {3.947342015266041*^9, 3.947342031293188*^9}, {
  3.9473420739742775`*^9, 
  3.9473420764726105`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"80caf38c-d81f-294a-bf37-\
8ab70fc8e59f"]
}, Open  ]],

